1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,560
Keep running along, watch as we pass by,
as we raise our flag, up high in the sky.

2
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:13,550
Alright,

3
00:00:13,633 --> 00:00:18,051
here we go now, sailing through the
endless ocean, facing all that comes by.

4
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:23,980
Let's look for our treasure nobody has
ever got to witness with their own eyes.

5
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:29,617
All we have to do is keep believing in our
dreams, And let our heart lead the way!

6
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:33,820
Then once we got all the
others left is to go,

7
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:39,217
When we face the dark and stormy weather?

8
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:42,177
Keep the pace, we'll
link our hearts together!

9
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:45,700
Then I'm sure we'll make it through!

10
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:47,757
No matter what!

11
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:51,457
Keep running along, keep running along!

12
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:54,397
Still raising our flag as we journey on!

13
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:59,537
Though our chances are close to
none, We won't back down from anyone!

14
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:03,457
Let's start off the chase,
let's start off the chase!

15
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:06,397
Toward our own dreams,
while keeping the pace!

16
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:08,757
With a compass pointing to our goal!

17
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:13,500
We won't stop till we've
gone around the world!

18
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:15,900
Start me up!

19
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:21,417
Keep running along, keep running along!

20
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:24,357
And we'll never stop,
till we're at the top!

21
00:01:24,440 --> 00:01:26,717
There's no way that we'll ever quit!

22
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:29,380
Won't keep heading for tomorrow!

23
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:33,437
Let's start up the chase,
let's start up the chase!

24
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:36,397
I see through your eyes
what we'll have to face!

25
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:39,017
All the memories we'll say in our hearts!

26
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:41,297
We'll never let them go!

27
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:43,360
Brand new world!

28
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:45,900
Let's start me up!

29
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:04,220
Too close!

30
00:02:05,780 --> 00:02:08,057
What's the deal with them
shooting their own ships?

31
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:09,280
Are they that dumb?

32
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:14,237
Oh great, I got small again!

33
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:17,737
Third gear is a pretty cool
idea and it is really powerful!

34
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:19,877
But talk about lousy side effects!

35
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:22,817
I was pumped up and
big for about a minute!

36
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:26,057
So I guess I'll He'll be
shrunk down for a minute, too.

37
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:29,964
I gotta hide till this wears off
or he'll stomp on me like a bug!

38
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:42,320
Is that a side effect or
some kind of bad joke?

39
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:44,761
Whatever it is, he's still alive.

40
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:49,626
Well, this would have been a waste of
time if he died in a measly cannon attack.

41
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:10,320
Look, everyone!

42
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:11,837
You can see the front gate!

43
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:13,820
We're almost there! Yeah!

44
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:17,220
Keep running!

45
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:22,117
You remember your old pal, Franky, right?

46
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:25,620
He got taken away by the
bad guys too, like Tom.

47
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:28,180
So you up for a fight or what?

48
00:03:45,060 --> 00:03:48,517
Your precious Straw Hat was
rampaging aboard that battleship,

49
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:50,306
and now he's a pile of ashes!

50
00:03:51,340 --> 00:03:52,697
Your captain is dead.

51
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:54,297
Go ahead and give up already!

52
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:55,757
What the hell?

53
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,937
That ship was filled with their own men.

54
00:03:58,020 --> 00:04:01,577
You're starting to understand the
merciless nature of the buster.

55
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:03,677
Call this is the face of justice.

56
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:04,837
Cutty Flam.

57
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:08,357
Now do yourself a favor
and hand over Nico Robin.

58
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:12,237
If you cooperate with us, I'll see to
it that you'll pardon for your crimes.

59
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:15,197
Why are you even bothering
to protect this woman?

60
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:17,037
Anyway, what's in it for you?

61
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:18,937
You're not even a pirate.

62
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:21,357
The world government is
devoted to protecting

63
00:04:21,440 --> 00:04:24,077
normal citizens like you
from people like her.

64
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:26,417
Do you really trust her more than us?

65
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:28,517
This woman with blood on her hands.

66
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:33,760
If you choose to defy us, well
you remember what happened to Tom.

67
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:35,550
AAAAAAAH!

68
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:36,870
OOH! OOH!

69
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:38,190
OOH!

70
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:41,297
My... face...

71
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:44,086
I didn't think I could
get any more swollen...

72
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:48,020
Aw, crap!

73
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:49,577
He's using the elephant sword!

74
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:51,077
That thing's unstoppable!

75
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:54,820
Okay, listen, Funnfried, this
has gone on for far too long.

76
00:04:55,140 --> 00:04:58,905
I want you to fatally wound
Mikko-Robin while her guard is down.

77
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:00,717
Take this!

78
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,340
Elevator!

79
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:08,580
Bastard!

80
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:21,700
He stopped it!

81
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:32,241
You just keep digging your
grave deeper and deeper

82
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:35,420
What are you doing, Von Freed?

83
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:36,737
You're an elephant, dammit!

84
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:37,797
How are you losing?

85
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:39,704
Get mad and slice them caprici!

86
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:44,677
You best make your nose
normal again, elephant?

87
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:48,995
Unless you want a couple of new
nostrils in the middle of your forehead!

88
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:51,850
Okay.

89
00:05:51,933 --> 00:05:53,500
Okay, there you go. Smart move.

90
00:05:54,260 --> 00:05:57,877
Nico Robin, you think Straw Hat
and the others are still coming?

91
00:05:57,960 --> 00:05:58,901
Without a doubt.

92
00:05:59,020 --> 00:05:59,961
They'll be here.

93
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:06,917
I already told you once before that
I'm betting everything on them Spanda.

94
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:07,830
You what?

95
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:09,550
Funny.

96
00:06:09,633 --> 00:06:12,087
I never dreamed this
day would actually come.

97
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:16,477
If I'd only had the power
before, it wouldn't even be here.

98
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:18,380
I'm amending the charges.

99
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:22,557
For the crime of designing and
building a ship for Gold Roger,

100
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:23,917
the king of the pirates,

101
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:27,824
Tom and Tom alone will be apprehended
and taken to Annie's lobby.

102
00:06:27,980 --> 00:06:29,060
That is all.

103
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:35,980
What in the hell got into that
old geezer's head? Whatever.

104
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:38,000
I don't need his lackeys.

105
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:40,165
Release those two apprentices!

106
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:48,360
Tom can't be saved from this.

107
00:06:49,640 --> 00:06:51,737
It's the government we're up against.

108
00:06:51,820 --> 00:06:54,460
There's nothing we can do. Endure it.

109
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:57,000
Tom traded his life for yours.

110
00:06:57,340 --> 00:06:58,977
If you make them your enemy,

111
00:06:59,060 --> 00:07:03,060
you won't be able to win, no matter
how many lives you have to give.

112
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:06,711
Benny's lobby is the government's
personal judicial island.

113
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:09,597
Not one single person who's been sent to

114
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:12,327
that dreadful place has
ever been seen again.

115
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:16,460
He's out of his mind!

116
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:17,913
What should we do, sir?

117
00:07:18,580 --> 00:07:20,345
Are you out of your mind, too?

118
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:21,600
We keep on going.

119
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:23,737
That's what he wants us to do, right?

120
00:07:23,820 --> 00:07:26,560
Don't worry about him. Right. Yes, sir.

121
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:31,494
All right, Puppetop, that's far enough.

122
00:07:33,880 --> 00:07:35,517
What do you think you're doing?

123
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:37,600
Where are you taking your creator?

124
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:49,060
Get him! Get him!

125
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:50,090
Get him!

126
00:07:50,173 --> 00:07:51,003
Get him!

127
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:53,900
I won't let you pass!

128
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:00,980
Give me Tom back!

129
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:08,233
Even if it killed me, I had
to stop them from taking Tom.

130
00:08:09,140 --> 00:08:11,728
Everyone knows the
reputation of any slobby.

131
00:08:12,080 --> 00:08:15,198
And everyone knows the power
of the world government.

132
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:19,180
But the Straw Hats didn't care.

133
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:23,226
They knew what they were up
against, and they still pressed on.

134
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:30,405
In order to save their friend,

135
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:34,464
they were willing to take on the
entire world without hesitation.

136
00:08:35,020 --> 00:08:36,726
And that's my kind of people.

137
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:45,593
I've never forgotten the role you
played in Tom's death, and I never will.

138
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:51,360
Every time I pictured your stupid
face, I dreamt of smashing it.

139
00:08:54,380 --> 00:08:55,580
Smashing your face!

140
00:08:55,860 --> 00:08:56,857
What are you doing?

141
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:57,937
Don't come any closer!

142
00:08:58,020 --> 00:08:58,850
Stop this!

143
00:08:58,933 --> 00:09:01,841
Until there was nothing
left but bloody hamburger!

144
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:21,168
That's a pretty good start.

145
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:25,386
Thanks to the Straw Hats, I
finally get to live out this dream.

146
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:31,620
How about some weapons?

147
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:38,180
I died before and it wasn't that bad.

148
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:41,057
I'll do whatever it takes to
get the Straw Hats out of here,

149
00:09:41,140 --> 00:09:43,728
even if it means me
dying for a second time.

150
00:09:52,620 --> 00:09:55,020
Hand over your escort ship right now.

151
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:58,400
I'm making them an escape
route and you're helping.

152
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:11,340
And I'm helping too.

153
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:12,700
I'm alright now.

154
00:10:20,980 --> 00:10:23,060
Don't look back. Just go.

155
00:10:23,380 --> 00:10:25,677
If you stay on this island, you'll die.

156
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:27,584
Take my raft and go out to sea.

157
00:10:27,820 --> 00:10:28,938
But what about you?

158
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:31,620
He's got me, little lady.

159
00:10:31,980 --> 00:10:34,980
I'm afraid this is the end. Hurry! No!

160
00:10:35,300 --> 00:10:37,480
Everybody I care about is here!

161
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:39,620
This is different.

162
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:41,397
This is nothing like Ohara.

163
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:44,197
And I've got nothing to
be afraid of this time.

164
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:46,200
I'm not alone. This time.

165
00:10:47,020 --> 00:10:48,480
I've got my friends.

166
00:10:57,380 --> 00:10:59,080
He sniffed me out.

167
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:03,240
So that power of yours
demands as much as it gives.

168
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:05,417
Seems like a pretty fair trade, though.

169
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:08,559
One must always pay a great
price for a great power.

170
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,180
Life returned paper art fighting for.

171
00:11:18,460 --> 00:11:19,780
FINGER PISTOLS!

172
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:29,280
Time to give up.

173
00:11:29,560 --> 00:11:32,913
If you continue these ridiculous
attacks, I'll have to...

174
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:44,000
I can't move!

175
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:46,580
Not good, dumb man.

176
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:51,640
I apologize, but I've got to
kill you in that stupid form.

177
00:11:52,100 --> 00:11:53,200
Now, die!

178
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:56,980
Finger pistol! Spots!

179
00:11:58,300 --> 00:11:59,620
Sheep's back body!

180
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:02,540
Come on, hurry up or we're gonna die!

181
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:18,740
That blow from earlier damaged my legs.

182
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:22,020
Hey, it's changing. I'm changing back.

183
00:12:33,580 --> 00:12:34,700
You see?

184
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:36,040
It worked.

185
00:12:36,620 --> 00:12:38,940
Looks like I messed you up after all.

186
00:12:53,180 --> 00:12:55,320
Is there really nothing we can do?

187
00:12:58,880 --> 00:13:00,704
I've got to think of something.

188
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:03,337
If I don't, then we're all going to drown.

189
00:13:03,420 --> 00:13:06,538
And we haven't even made
sure that Robin is safe yet.

190
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:08,680
Is this really the end?

191
00:13:08,940 --> 00:13:11,577
I suppose I have lived a good life.

192
00:13:11,660 --> 00:13:14,837
There's no denying that
I've had some fun times.

193
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,837
No, I'm not ready to die!

194
00:13:16,920 --> 00:13:18,337
I can't drown in a tunnel.

195
00:13:18,420 --> 00:13:21,477
This is not a fitting gift for
the brave warrior of the sea.

196
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:22,420
Usam.

197
00:13:24,180 --> 00:13:26,700
I can't hold my breath any longer.

198
00:13:28,620 --> 00:13:30,400
It hurts too much.

199
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:32,797
Everything's starting to go dark.

200
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:34,440
Someone help!

201
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:36,117
It's alright.

202
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,977
Just hang in there.

203
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:40,140
I'm not going to let you die.

204
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:43,690
What?

205
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:44,940
What's going on?

206
00:13:45,380 --> 00:13:47,660
It feels like something's pulling me.

207
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:01,180
Am I hallucinating?

208
00:14:01,940 --> 00:14:03,360
That's gotta be it.

209
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:09,555
It's just like those old
tales that sailors talk about.

210
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:13,580
Just before they drown, they
see an elegant tail fin.

211
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:19,780
They look up, surprised
to see long, flowing hair.

212
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:24,080
I've never seen anything so beautiful.

213
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:27,252
It's like she's something out of a dream.

214
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:29,100
A legendary mermaid.

215
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:34,520
If I'm dying, and this is just a dream,

216
00:14:36,020 --> 00:14:37,437
then I don't want to wake up.

217
00:14:37,520 --> 00:14:39,737
I'm running as fast as
this tail will let me!

218
00:14:39,820 --> 00:14:42,232
None of you are going to die on my watch!

219
00:14:50,140 --> 00:14:51,199
She's the mermaid!

220
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:14,657
Sorry, boys, but me and the Straw
Hats will be taking this boat.

221
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:16,564
Gotta escape somehow, you know?

222
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:22,070
And so,

223
00:15:22,260 --> 00:15:26,897
after cleaning house a bit, what was once
an escort ship is now our escape ship.

224
00:15:26,980 --> 00:15:27,810
Handy.

225
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:29,150
Now we wait.

226
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:31,495
Once the others get here, we'll split.

227
00:15:42,260 --> 00:15:43,480
What's that?

228
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:45,680
Everyone!

229
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:51,240
Don't you die on me?

230
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:08,350
Hurry!

231
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:11,680
The main gates are just ahead!

232
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:13,666
We're almost off this island!

233
00:16:14,020 --> 00:16:16,440
It shows a little further! Run, Giants!

234
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:17,657
Give it all you've got!

235
00:16:17,740 --> 00:16:19,180
Just leave it to us!

236
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:23,144
We can finally get out of here!

237
00:16:23,320 --> 00:16:24,500
We're gonna be safe!

238
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:31,680
Be to the other side!

239
00:16:32,060 --> 00:16:32,940
Giant doors!

240
00:16:33,140 --> 00:16:35,905
Don't do nothing when
you've got giant muscles!

241
00:16:47,980 --> 00:16:51,717
Three freaking battleships
must have been waiting for us.

242
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:53,677
Look, they made it out.

243
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:54,837
How'd they get free?

244
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:56,857
We left them tied up in the courthouse.

245
00:16:56,940 --> 00:16:58,377
They're stronger than we thought.

246
00:16:58,460 --> 00:17:00,297
Vice admiral, sir.

247
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:01,277
I know.

248
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:04,060
Aim the cannons at them. Sir,

249
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:06,457
state your unit, your marine code,

250
00:17:06,540 --> 00:17:09,697
and have your picture ID ready to
show before you can board the ship?

251
00:17:09,780 --> 00:17:11,120
You're good. Go on.

252
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:12,440
Oh, what a relief.

253
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:15,485
I thought we were gonna
go down with the island

254
00:17:27,860 --> 00:17:30,057
Resistance is futile, pirates.

255
00:17:30,140 --> 00:17:33,660
You make one move, and
we'll empty our ammo on you.

256
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:36,540
This couldn't get any worse! Oh, man.

257
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:38,637
I doubt they're gonna offer us amnesty.

258
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,955
And we can't go back.

259
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:41,097
The island's burning.

260
00:17:41,180 --> 00:17:42,877
We've got nowhere we can run to.

261
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:46,400
Every one of their weapons,
all of them, aimed at us!

262
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,882
So what's going through
your head right now, huh?

263
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:54,440
I'm thinking back on my life.

264
00:17:55,580 --> 00:17:57,286
You shouldn't talk like that.

265
00:17:57,440 --> 00:17:59,380
It's either that, or what.

266
00:18:01,020 --> 00:18:02,400
What comes next?

267
00:18:02,640 --> 00:18:03,500
The afterlife.

268
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:05,290
Get out!

269
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:13,560
All of our remaining
personnel have boarded.

270
00:18:13,820 --> 00:18:16,980
All ships, retreat to
a safe firing distance.

271
00:18:17,360 --> 00:18:19,948
They're not really going
to shoot us, right?

272
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:30,860
Sir, battleships 6,

273
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:33,157
7 and 8 have identified
and reported a large

274
00:18:33,240 --> 00:18:36,240
number of pirates located
in front of the main gate

275
00:18:40,100 --> 00:18:43,960
Hey, all of you, wake up!
Come on! Say something!

276
00:18:57,120 --> 00:18:58,020
They made it.

277
00:18:58,200 --> 00:18:59,612
They're all still alive.

278
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:00,700
It's a miracle.

279
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:02,158
I can't believe it.

280
00:19:02,320 --> 00:19:05,597
They must have seen something down there
that put them all in a state of shock.

281
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:07,637
Whatever it was, it saved their lives.

282
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:12,297
If they hadn't passed out, they would
have swallowed enough water to kill them.

283
00:19:12,380 --> 00:19:14,615
Well, either way, they're still alive.

284
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:18,617
Though it does make you
wonder what they could

285
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:21,317
have seen down there that
spooked them so much?

286
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:22,860
I bet it was you!

287
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:29,597
Well, Lock there.

288
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:33,915
You're the one that pirate king boy
wanted to rescue so bad, aren't you?

289
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:36,117
Yeah, I remember now.

290
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:38,080
We met at the ship station.

291
00:19:40,060 --> 00:19:42,178
These Straw Hats are something else.

292
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:47,077
Back then, I never would have thought you
guys could pull off a stunt like this.

293
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:50,477
If you don't hurry up and put some damn
clothes on, I'll gouge my eyes out.

294
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:54,537
When he said he was going to be king of
the pirates, I gotta admit, I laughed.

295
00:19:54,620 --> 00:19:57,260
Our Gourmet is counting on us!

296
00:19:57,440 --> 00:19:58,600
We're leaving now!

297
00:19:59,360 --> 00:20:03,419
But now after everything that's
happened, I bet he can actually do it

298
00:20:13,660 --> 00:20:14,490
Is...

299
00:20:14,573 --> 00:20:15,403
is Nami okay?

300
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:17,820
As lively as ever.

301
00:20:18,060 --> 00:20:19,178
You guys are tough.

302
00:20:19,860 --> 00:20:21,860
Welcome to the land of the living.

303
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:25,840
It wasn't a nightmare!

304
00:20:26,160 --> 00:20:27,807
Mermaids really don't exist!

305
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:31,097
So all those old sailor stories are true.

306
00:20:31,180 --> 00:20:33,917
Every time you think you see a
mermaid, it's actually a dugong.

307
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:34,997
Shut up, you bastard.

308
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:37,537
She hasn't even confessed
to being a mermaid yet.

309
00:20:37,620 --> 00:20:39,197
Stop trying to kill my fantasies.

310
00:20:39,280 --> 00:20:42,339
If you want to be specific,
I'm an ice fish mermaid.

311
00:20:42,780 --> 00:20:43,610
Stop it!

312
00:20:43,693 --> 00:20:44,857
Don't say another word!

313
00:20:44,940 --> 00:20:45,940
There's no way!

314
00:20:46,140 --> 00:20:49,728
What kind of mermaid lives on
dry land and has legs and feet?

315
00:20:51,380 --> 00:20:53,740
I refuse to accept this!

316
00:20:55,340 --> 00:20:59,557
Just to educate you boys, when we
mermaids get to be about 30 years old,

317
00:20:59,640 --> 00:21:03,837
our tail fin forks in two and we can
walk on land like a regular old human.

318
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:07,377
If you ever make it out to Fishman
Island, you'll see what I'm talking about.

319
00:21:07,460 --> 00:21:08,460
Their tail split?

320
00:21:08,880 --> 00:21:09,710
Oh, I get it.

321
00:21:09,793 --> 00:21:12,757
I heard the same thing happens to a
cat's tail if they live to be a hundred.

322
00:21:12,840 --> 00:21:14,297
Then they become goblins.

323
00:21:14,380 --> 00:21:16,380
Ah, so she's a goblin cat.

324
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:19,089
Don't lump mermaids in
with those monsters.

325
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:21,099
Enough about that.

326
00:21:21,220 --> 00:21:22,137
Where are your manners?

327
00:21:22,220 --> 00:21:23,985
Didn't I just save your lives?

328
00:21:24,980 --> 00:21:26,420
Thank you, Granny Kaku.

329
00:21:26,840 --> 00:21:28,100
We appreciate it.

330
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,100
Don't mention it.

331
00:21:55,880 --> 00:21:59,137
Oh, what happened where am I?

332
00:21:59,220 --> 00:22:05,497
Yes,

333
00:22:05,580 --> 00:22:09,560
because of all of you!

334
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:11,557
Thank you so much!

335
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:15,637
I

336
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:22,720
always

337
00:22:24,400 --> 00:22:25,230
did

338
00:22:25,313 --> 00:22:26,143
think it was weird

339
00:22:26,226 --> 00:22:27,056
that you have fins and scales.

340
00:22:27,139 --> 00:22:27,969
Now I know why!

341
00:22:28,052 --> 00:22:29,697
How many clues does it take?

342
00:22:29,780 --> 00:22:32,357
Hey, what's wrong?

343
00:22:32,440 --> 00:22:34,077
Are you all right?

344
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:35,197
I...

345
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:39,120
I can't move my body.

346
00:22:39,540 --> 00:22:40,660
I'm not surprised.

347
00:22:41,140 --> 00:22:42,357
Don't worry about it.

348
00:22:42,440 --> 00:22:44,558
I'll explain everything later, okay?

349
00:22:48,080 --> 00:22:49,180
Hey, Zoro!

350
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:08,270
Zoro!

351
00:23:08,353 --> 00:23:10,080
I mean, uh, swordsman!

352
00:23:12,800 --> 00:23:14,153
Over here, take a look.

353
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:25,346
Hard to believe that's the same
island we were on not long ago.

354
00:23:27,360 --> 00:23:28,400
What's going on?

355
00:23:28,560 --> 00:23:29,757
What's up with this attack?

356
00:23:29,840 --> 00:23:31,958
It's like a sea of flames out there!

357
00:23:35,740 --> 00:23:37,220
I noticed something else.

358
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:41,972
It seems kind of like they're trying
to avoid firing where Nico Robin's at.

359
00:23:42,100 --> 00:23:45,688
That would explain why this
bridge hasn't been blown to bits.

360
00:23:47,660 --> 00:23:51,477
If they don't want to kill her, then
they still intend on getting her back.

361
00:23:51,560 --> 00:23:54,437
After the Marines are done
attacking Eni's lobby,

362
00:23:54,520 --> 00:23:58,537
they'll probably come after us with
some hand-to-hand combat to reclaim her.

363
00:23:58,620 --> 00:23:59,877
I don't like the sound of that.

364
00:23:59,960 --> 00:24:00,977
We're at our limit here.

365
00:24:01,060 --> 00:24:01,942
On top of that,

366
00:24:02,040 --> 00:24:05,117
those battleships are bound to have
some pretty powerful guys on board.

367
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:06,612
Where's Luffy right now?

368
00:24:07,020 --> 00:24:09,337
From where I last saw him
and what's left standing,

369
00:24:09,420 --> 00:24:12,420
I'd say he's there, the
first tower of that bridge.

370
00:24:21,660 --> 00:24:23,719
He's fighting that damn pigeon guy.

371
00:24:23,880 --> 00:24:25,200
You know, Rob Lucci.

372
00:24:25,740 --> 00:24:26,780
That's close by.

373
00:24:26,980 --> 00:24:28,274
We should go help him.

374
00:24:29,260 --> 00:24:30,090
No, don't bother.

375
00:24:30,173 --> 00:24:32,797
That pigeon bastard he's
fighting is no ordinary man.

376
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:34,351
No good could come of it.

377
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:38,031
If we get caught up in that
mess, who knows what'll happen.

378
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:46,597
Those battleships could
turn this way at any time.

379
00:24:46,680 --> 00:24:49,680
We need to make sure we
still have an escape route.

380
00:24:50,080 --> 00:24:52,668
The plan is to stay
here and wait for Luffy.

381
00:24:52,980 --> 00:24:54,400
It's the best we can do.

382
00:25:06,380 --> 00:25:08,360
The storm is just beginning.

383
00:25:09,860 --> 00:25:10,690
Understood.

384
00:25:23,560 --> 00:25:25,000
Hey, Franky.

385
00:25:25,700 --> 00:25:27,347
Think your friends are okay?

386
00:25:29,920 --> 00:25:31,200
Are you serious?

387
00:25:31,580 --> 00:25:33,557
Nothing can stop the Franky family.

388
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:34,740
Don't you worry.

389
00:25:34,960 --> 00:25:36,313
I'm sure they got away.

390
00:25:40,480 --> 00:25:41,740
Hey! Paulie!

391
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:42,998
What are you doing?

392
00:25:46,740 --> 00:25:48,140
A transponder snail?

393
00:25:48,400 --> 00:25:50,117
What the hell are you
going to do with that?

394
00:25:50,200 --> 00:25:53,376
We need to find out how the
Straw Hats are holding up.

395
00:25:57,820 --> 00:26:00,200
Big Brow! No!

396
00:26:26,720 --> 00:26:29,000
This is gonna be the last time!

397
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:33,280
I won't stop until I bring you down.

398
00:26:33,500 --> 00:26:36,357
You hear me your body
can't take this you'll kill

399
00:26:36,440 --> 00:26:40,920
yourself Maybe I guess there's
only one way to find out.

400
00:26:45,640 --> 00:26:47,300
Now second gear
